    "turn_text": "This is AgriPulse Open Mike. I'm your host, Jeff Nolly. Our guest this week is main First District representative, Shelley Pingree. AgriPulse Open Mike is brought to you by Syngenta and their well-being portal. Syngenta believes we are all stronger together. AgriPulse Open Mike continues with Congresswoman Shelley Pingree next. During this unprecedented time, Senjenta offers resources to protect more than crops. Senjenta's well-being portal connects people to ways to stay healthy and active, manage stress, and enjoy more of life. To access the portal, click the link in the Adriples. and gentle believes we're all stronger together. This is Agropulse Open Mike. As a member of the House Committees on Appropriations and Agriculture, Maine U.S. Representative Shelley Pingree says Washington leadership had no choice but to respond to the immense challenge facing the nation from the COVID-19 pandemic. And while she supports the concept of some of the relief efforts from the Department of Agriculture, she says they haven't worked for her constituents.",
