  {
    "episode_id": 72711,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72711.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, I was in a committee hearing where Chairman Peterson said that, and honestly it was music to my ears. We've had a very limited committee schedule this year, mostly just working through the subcommittees, not done a lot of comprehensive evaluation of programs at the USDA or the system. And I really appreciated him being able to stand back and say, there is something going wrong here with our system. He was talking about, obviously he's in a district where a lot of hogs have to be slaughtered and buried and destroyed because they didn't have the capacity in the slaughterhouses. You know, I feel for him. You watch that every day or you see your farmers going through that and suddenly you're starting to say, you know, what's wrong with this picture? We got lines at the food banks and we're destroying food. And I think he does feel like it's time for Congress to step up, to better understand how the system works, to have more of a say in the distribution of this money. And, you know, that's an easy sell for me. I would love to see our committee do some real hard work that it's a wonderful committee we come from you know such diverse parts of the country we represent all political views but there's a lot of common ground about uh... protecting our farmers about not having you know too much bureaucracy of getting food to hungry people i i think there would be a lot of common ground and i think it would really serve us well at this moment in time to stand back and say uh... you know the spook system did not serve us well uh... the supply chain you know it falls apart if you can't If you have a shutdown in the slaughterhouses or suddenly restaurants aren't buying the food that you were intended for restaurants, so the things that are packaged in that side, you've got to throw them away or you can't get them to consumers. I was thrilled. I really appreciate Colin stepping up and saying that's a good idea. I can't wait.",
